    {
      "id": "j30mkq9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "12.5 Important Boundary Disputes and Sensitivities"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7xl6i8w",
      "content": "Arunachal Pradesh is at the centre of India's most significant border dispute with China. Key points for examination:"
    },
    {
      "id": "ihvckhz",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "China officially refers to most of Arunachal Pradesh as 'Zangnan' (South Tibet) and claims it as part of Chinese territory.",
        "The McMahon Line (1914) is accepted by India as the international boundary but rejected by China.",
        "The Tawang district is of particular importance to China as it contains the Tawang Monastery, which has historic links to Tibetan Buddhism.",
        "India has been significantly upgrading infrastructure (roads, tunnels, advanced landing grounds) along the LAC.",
        "Galwan Valley clash (2020) in Ladakh heightened focus on overall border management including Arunachal.",
        "China has renamed several places in Arunachal Pradesh unilaterally — India has consistently rejected these renamings."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cshuhu9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
